# .gitignore — Jumping Squares
#
# This project is intentionally text-only (HTML/CSS/JS + Markdown), with no
# build step and no dependencies. The entries below keep OS/editor cruft and
# any future tooling artefacts out of the repository.

# --- OS-generated files ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# --- Editor / IDE ------------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.bak
*.tmp
.idea/
.vscode/
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project

# --- Logs & debug output -----------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- Node.js (only relevant if tooling/tests-with-deps are added later) ------
node_modules/
package-lock.json.bak
.npm/
.cache/
coverage/

# --- Environment / secrets (defensive; none expected in this project) --------
.env
.env.*
*.local

# --- Binary files ------------------------------------------------------------
# The repo is text-only for now. Ignore common binary/media types by default so
# nothing large sneaks in. When an images folder is added later, add a negated
# exception INSIDE that folder to allow its assets, e.g. create images/.gitignore:
#
#     # images/.gitignore
#     !*.png
#     !*.svg
#     !*.webp
#
# ...or un-ignore specific paths here with lines like:
#     !images/**/*.png
#
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.ico
*.mp3
*.wav
*.ogg
*.zip
*.tar
*.gz
